 :seon.program/shapes
 [:map-of
  {:description
   "The derived program-row shapes one operation owns its rows by, keyed by
    identity attribute (seon.program/shapes-in derives them from a declaration
    population). An operation resolves its population ONCE and hands THIS value
    to every per-row question, so the declaration world cannot be re-resolved
    per row. It is a distinct schema from the population itself: a population's
    keys are ordinary attribute keywords, so handing one where shapes are
    expected is a typed refusal instead of a row silently stripped of every
    attribute its family owns."}
  :seon.program/identity-attribute :seon.program/shape]
